                                                                  7728 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     7728 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        7728 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     7728 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     7728 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            7728 1451
                                                                  7728 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           7728 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         7728 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR7728 1451
       expands from 0 to 5.436799E+1 eV. A total of               7728 1451
       2 l-values are used and 88 resonances. The resonance       7728 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              7728 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       7728 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          7728 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     7728 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    7728 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  7728 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   7728 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          7728 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       7728 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    7728 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       7728 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         7728 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 0.6671 eV and          7728 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0001495 1e-4.             7728 1451
                                                                  7728 1451
       After the ladder method, the retroactive method is applied 7728 1451
       to update the MF32 and MF2 with the SAMMY code.            7728 1451
                                                                  7728 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  7728 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    7728 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    7728 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   7728 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    7728 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              7728 1451
        SAMMY is used in the retroactive mode to update MF32.     7728 1451
                                                                  7728 1451
